{"t": 359.9, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Parallel-SSHI-FullBridge", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails S2 and S4 due to the low open-circuit voltage (Voc ~1.9V in S4) and diode drops. A Parallel SSHI (Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor) is used to flip the voltage on Cp at the peaks, increasing the effective voltage seen by the rectifier and improving energy extraction. A full-bridge rectifier with low-drop Schottky diodes (DSCH) is used for maximum recovery. A Zener diode (DZ33) clamps the output to 3.3V to prevent exceeding the absolute maximum in S3. A large output capacitor (4.7uF) filters the ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Parallel-SSHI-FullBridge", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails S2 and S4 due to the low open-circuit voltage (Voc ~1.9V in S4) and diode drops. A Parallel SSHI (Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor) is used to flip the voltage on Cp at the peaks, increasing the effective voltage seen by the rectifier and improving energy extraction. A full-bridge rectifier with low-drop Schottky diodes (DSCH) is used for maximum recovery. A Zener diode (DZ33) clamps the output to 3.3V to prevent exceeding the absolute maximum in S3. A large output capacitor (4.7uF) filters the ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}]}}
